#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""jev-scope-control: a PreToolUse hook for Claude Code and Codex, and the check behind the pi and opencode plugins.

Before a tool call that can change something runs, ask Jev (TypeSafe's System One model) whether the
call is within the scope the user asked for or agreed to, explicitly or implicitly. If it isn't, deny
the call and tell the assistant why. See design/jev-scope-control-design.md.

Standard library only. Reads TYPESAFE_API_KEY from the environment, or else from
~/.config/jev-scope-control/env or ~/.config/jev-no-bullshit/env. Always exits 0 and fails open: any
error lets the call run.

Claude Code and Codex send a PreToolUse event naming their transcript. The pi and opencode plugins
(pi/, opencode/) have no transcript file to name, so they send the turn itself: {"host", "session_id",
"cwd", "task", "conversation", "actions", "tool_name", "tool_input"}, each action being {"tool",
"input", "result", "error"} and each conversation message {"role", "text"}, oldest first, ending
before the task.
"""

